From: Omarchy Mobile <omamobile@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8953-xiaomi-markw: float the battery at 4.35 V

Not for upstream as it stands: a bring-up test (BRINGUP-CHARGER.md C4).

With the 4.38 V float, the PMI8950 charger latches a battery
overvoltage (batt-ov) at the top of each charge, at 4.35-4.37 V by the
fuel gauge and right after termination, and charging stays stopped
until the charge path restarts. Float at 4.35 V to see whether batt-ov
tracks the float or sits at a fixed level.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8953-xiaomi-markw.dts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8953-xiaomi-markw.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8953-xiaomi-markw.dts
@@ -140,7 +140,7 @@
 	charge-full-design-microamp-hours = <4000000>;
 	constant-charge-current-max-microamp = <1000000>;
 	voltage-min-design-microvolt = <3400000>;
-	voltage-max-design-microvolt = <4380000>;
+	voltage-max-design-microvolt = <4350000>;
 };
 
 &camss {
